{"tool_name":"saucie","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"SAUCIE","home":"https://github.com/KrishnaswamyLab/SAUCIE/","license":"Not licensed","summary":"SAUCIE is a python object that loads data from a numpy matrix and produces numpy matrix output for the reconstruction, visualization, and/or clusters.","addition_date":"2019-10-13T15:01:04Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:01:37.309543Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:SAUCIE","cost":"Free of charge","documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/KrishnaswamyLab/SAUCIE/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"}]}],"note":"Input should contain single-cell measurements, such as mass cytometry or single-cell RNA sequencing data.","operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"Statistical modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3664"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2082"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"SAUCIE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-019-0576-7","metadata":{"abstract":"It is currently challenging to analyze single-cell data consisting of many cells and samples, and to address variations arising from batch effects and different sample preparations. For this purpose, we present SAUCIE, a deep neural network that combines parallelization and scalability offered by neural networks, with the deep representation of data that can be learned by them to perform many single-cell data analysis tasks. Our regularizations (penalties) render features learned in hidden layers of the neural network interpretable. On large, multi-patient datasets, SAUCIE\u2019s various hidden layers contain denoised and batch-corrected data, a low-dimensional visualization and unsupervised clustering, as well as other information that can be used to explore the data. We analyze a 180-sample dataset consisting of 11 million T cells from dengue patients in India, measured with mass cytometry. SAUCIE can batch correct and identify cluster-based signatures of acute dengue infection and create a patient manifold, stratifying immune response to dengue.","authors":[{"name":"Amodio M."},{"name":"Campbell A."},{"name":"Chen W.S."},{"name":"Desai A."},{"name":"Krishnaswamy S."},{"name":"Kumar P."},{"name":"Mohsen H."},{"name":"Montgomery R."},{"name":"Moon K.R."},{"name":"Ravi V."},{"name":"Srinivasan K."},{"name":"Venkataswamy M."},{"name":"Wang X."},{"name":"Wolf G."},{"name":"Zhao Y."},{"name":"van Dijk D."}],"citationCount":183,"date":"2019-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Exploring single-cell data with deep multitasking neural networks"},"pmcid":"PMC10164410","pmid":"31591579","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SAUCIE","home":"https://bio.tools/SAUCIE","license":"Not licensed","summary":"SAUCIE is a python object that loads data from a numpy matrix and produces numpy matrix output for the reconstruction, visualization, and/or clusters.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:saucie/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source